    {
        "desc": "Specks of dirt and granite flakes, from the path to the north, have drifted down\nthe hillside and cover the northern side of this narrow walkway. A large tree\nhas fallen diagonally across the walkway and continues on to hang over the cliff\nto the south. Tangled in the branches are the remains of a wrought iron railing\nthat once warned weary travellers of the abrupt edge. From its size the tree\nappears to be at least a thousand years old. An odd place for a tree to have\ngrown so close, this one obviously took root and died all in the interim of time\npassed since this city's downfall.\n",
