    {
        "desc": "Several broken stone bookcases lie on their sides having been knocked down\nagainst the west wall. Elven words carved in some rounded stone posts that once\nstood at the end of each bookshelf seem to denote an ancient filing system.\nLying on the floor are the remains of several stone boxes about the size of a\nlarge journal. It would have taken a rather strong person to have lifted these\nheavy stone containers high enough to have cracked them open against the floor\nexposing the manuscripts inside. Brown flaky dust covers the floor along with\nsome small brass fasteners, apparently all that is left of this library's\ncontents, eroded into nothingness over the course of centuries.\n",
